place in Austin, Texas,

00:46:02.850 --> 00:46:05.460
or, I forget, somewhere
in Texas, I don't know.

00:46:05.460 --> 00:46:07.830
And yeah, we just had to
make a little video there

00:46:07.830 --> 00:46:08.663
and put it out,

00:46:08.663 --> 00:46:09.496
we didn't even put it on our main channel,

00:46:09.496 --> 00:46:10.623
our second channel,

00:46:10.623 --> 00:46:13.200
They paid us like a couple
thousand or something,

00:46:13.200 --> 00:46:15.390
and it was like, you know,
that was our first sponsor.

00:46:15.390 --> 00:46:17.220
- Was the reception to that though?

00:46:17.220 --> 00:46:19.079
- What the fuck is this?

00:46:19.079 --> 00:46:21.990
(all laughing)

00:46:21.990 --> 00:46:23.280
- YouTube seems so wild.

00:46:23.280 --> 00:46:24.914
- Yeah, yeah.
- Weirdest shit.

00:46:24.914 --> 00:46:27.450
- There were absolutely no rules.

00:46:27.450 --> 00:46:29.700
And I remember when I first started,

00:46:29.700 --> 00:46:33.180
I would actually go out
of my way to break rules

00:46:33.180 --> 00:46:36.390
to show YouTube that this
rule could be broken.

00:46:36.390 --> 00:46:38.100
I'm just a bad boy.

00:46:38.100 --> 00:46:39.225
- Like what?

00:46:39.225 --> 00:46:41.100
- And one thing that I realized

00:46:41.100 --> 00:46:43.473
is that there was this channel that,

00:46:44.760 --> 00:46:46.080
I can't remember what the name of it was,

00:46:46.080 --> 00:46:48.741
in fact, it's probably better
that I don't say the name.

00:46:48.741 --> 00:46:52.470
They had videos that would just pop off,

00:46:52.470 --> 00:46:53.970
but they'd have like, 12 comments.

00:46:53.970 --> 00:46:57.750
And I was like, this math doesn't add up.

00:46:57.750 --> 00:46:59.520
And of course, as an 18-year-old kid,

00:46:59.520 --> 00:47:01.203
I was like, I must get
down to the bottom of this.

00:47:01.203 --> 00:47:02.403
It's my duty!

00:47:03.570 --> 00:47:04.740
- Internet detective mode.

00:47:04.740 --> 00:47:05.910
- Yeah, yeah.

00:47:05.910 --> 00:47:10.230
- So I did a test on our MySpace

00:47:10.230 --> 00:47:13.590
and it was kind of what I learned

00:47:13.590 --> 00:47:17.580
from that other company doing
the hidden iframe thing.

00:47:17.580 --> 00:47:22.580
So I realized on MySpace you
can hide an iframe as well.

00:47:22.890 --> 00:47:24.090
Which is ridiculous to think

00:47:24.090 --> 00:47:27.270
that anyone could have any
page load in the background.

00:47:27.270 --> 00:47:32.100
So I hid it on our page and
I realized that that worked.

00:47:32.100 --> 00:47:34.740
So I said, "YouTube, fix this."

00:47:34.740 --> 00:47:37.650
I don't know if it was even me saying it,

00:47:37.650 --> 00:47:40.140
but also a big thing was that that channel

00:47:40.140 --> 00:47:45.013
was also having hundreds of
thousands of new subscribers.

00:47:45.013 --> 00:47:48.180
I think it was right when
they announced subscribing.

00:47:48.180 --> 00:47:49.290
And I was like,

00:47:49.290 --> 00:47:51.210
how is this channel that
gets so little comments

00:47:51.210 --> 00:47:52.950
having so many views and subscribers?

00:47:52.950 --> 00:47:57.330
So I also hid an iframe on our MySpace,

00:47:57.330 --> 00:48:00.150
that auto-subscribed
people to our channel.

00:48:00.150 --> 00:48:03.750
And after a day, I was like,
"Ee, yeah, this is gross,

00:48:03.750 --> 00:48:05.280
I'm not gonna have this on here."

00:48:05.280 --> 00:48:09.210
So I removed it, we got like
100, 200 new subscribers,

00:48:09.210 --> 00:48:10.950
I felt gross about it.

00:48:10.950 --> 00:48:13.290
And I think in order
to repent for my sins,

00:48:13.290 --> 00:48:15.210
I went to YouTube and I was like,

00:48:15.210 --> 00:48:18.810
this is a way that people
are cheating the system.

00:48:18.810 --> 00:48:21.690
So then YouTube within
the next couple days added

00:48:21.690 --> 00:48:23.460
