01:52:10.680 --> 01:52:12.870
Vine was like, we're
coming back with Vine 2.

01:52:12.870 --> 01:52:14.629
- And then TikTok was like, nah.

01:52:14.629 --> 01:52:15.995
- Yeah, TikTok was like, no, we got this,

01:52:15.995 --> 01:52:18.060
we got this, don't worry.
- We're way ahead of you!

01:52:18.060 --> 01:52:19.097
- Well, I find it really weird,

01:52:19.097 --> 01:52:23.367
'cause I feel like now
TikTok is what YouTube was

01:52:23.367 --> 01:52:25.863
10, 15 years ago.
- True, true.

01:52:25.863 --> 01:52:28.740
- Remember when in back
in the day where YouTubers

01:52:28.740 --> 01:52:30.360
would try to get on TV,

01:52:30.360 --> 01:52:31.800
which was like the old media,

01:52:31.800 --> 01:52:33.540
in order to legitimize themselves.

01:52:33.540 --> 01:52:36.870
And now it's TikTokers
trying to become YouTubers

01:52:36.870 --> 01:52:38.197
in order to-
- Oh, for sure.

01:52:38.197 --> 01:52:39.450
- To legitimize themselves.
- To legitimize themselves.

01:52:39.450 --> 01:52:42.450
And it's been so weird just
seeing that transition.

01:52:42.450 --> 01:52:44.130
- That's so true.

01:52:44.130 --> 01:52:47.403
I guess it's because the
platform is so easily accessible.

01:52:47.403 --> 01:52:49.650
Like you were saying that
anyone could jump on there

01:52:49.650 --> 01:52:52.650
and you can build an audience on there,

01:52:52.650 --> 01:52:54.540
people can find you, the
algorithm is very good.

01:52:54.540 --> 01:52:57.240
