02:00:01.050 --> 02:00:03.480
So that has given me a lot of confidence

02:00:03.480 --> 02:00:05.160
in the direction of that,

02:00:05.160 --> 02:00:06.630
because monetization was a huge issue.

02:00:06.630 --> 02:00:08.070
Every time I'd upload for a while,

02:00:08.070 --> 02:00:10.230
I was like, mm, I don't know, let's see,

02:00:10.230 --> 02:00:12.870
this thing I put tens of
thousands of dollars into,

02:00:12.870 --> 02:00:15.210
it might be worth nothing.

02:00:15.210 --> 02:00:18.111
I might just could be in the red for this.

02:00:18.111 --> 02:00:19.200
They did fix some things I feel,

02:00:19.200 --> 02:00:20.850
and they're slowly but surely I think

02:00:20.850 --> 02:00:23.220
fixing a lot of the glaring issues.

02:00:23.220 --> 02:00:26.490
- Was there like a point
where this changed from,

02:00:26.490 --> 02:00:29.610
because as with the way
being a content creator is,

02:00:29.610 --> 02:00:32.820
this changed from being a job to a career?

02:00:32.820 --> 02:00:36.570
Because for the longest time,
I treated YouTube as a job

02:00:36.570 --> 02:00:37.890
because you wake up and you're like,

02:00:37.890 --> 02:00:41.070
maybe I'll be irrelevant
tomorrow, a week from now, a year.

02:00:41.070 --> 02:00:43.980
And I didn't really feel
like this was a career

02:00:43.980 --> 02:00:45.960
literally until this
podcast when I'm just like,

02:00:45.960 --> 02:00:48.690
oh, okay, this is like
a sustainable business

02:00:48.690 --> 02:00:51.858
that I can see myself 5,
10 years in the future.

02:00:51.858 --> 02:00:53.910
Was there a point for that for you?

02:00:53.910 --> 02:00:55.980
- I think the moment that that changes

02:00:55.980 --> 02:00:57.120
with somebody in general

02:00:57.120 --> 02:00:58.740
is probably when you have a format

02:00:58.740 --> 02:01:00.960
that you can come back
to and feel confident in,

02:01:00.960 --> 02:01:03.060
and that's probably why
this podcast was like,

02:01:03.060 --> 02:01:06.510
we know the format, it's
kind of all figured out

02:01:06.510 --> 02:01:09.445
so that it feels like
this is a repeating thing.

02:01:09.445 --> 02:01:14.028
For me it was, I think it
probably felt like career

02:01:14.028 --> 02:01:16.590
when we were purchased by Defy,

02:01:16.590 --> 02:01:18.420
because it was like-

02:01:18.420 --> 02:01:19.430
- Salary.
- Salary.

02:01:19.430 --> 02:01:22.893
I mean, that kind of I feel
like it was unique to me though.

02:01:23.880 --> 02:01:28.020
But then after that,
going off independently,

02:01:28.020 --> 02:01:30.360
the moment that it felt
like a career for me now

02:01:30.360 --> 02:01:32.520
was when I had a series,
"I Spent A Day With,"

02:01:32.520 --> 02:01:33.500
to go back to.

02:01:33.500 --> 02:01:34.893
I knew that it was a repeating thing.

02:01:34.893 --> 02:01:37.680
- Like a safety net, like
something comfort, you know?

02:01:37.680 --> 02:01:38.870
- I think that's the difference,

02:01:38.870 --> 02:01:41.400
when you know that you have something,

02:01:41.400 --> 02:01:44.190
you're not starting from
square one every single video.

02:01:44.190 --> 02:01:45.753
A lot of people are still
trying to figure out

02:01:45.753 --> 02:01:46.680
what they're doing,

02:01:46.680 --> 02:01:48.780
so every single video is
back to the drawing board

02:01:48.780 --> 02:01:50.100
and then that just feels like a job,

02:01:50.100 --> 02:01:51.120
and trust me, it's tough.

02:01:51.120 --> 02:01:52.500
- Yeah, because I feel like

02:01:52.500 --> 02:01:53.850
when you're starting off a YouTube,

02:01:53.850 --> 02:01:56.610
you want to make every
video a 10 out 10 banger.

02:01:56.610 --> 02:01:57.930
You wanna be motivated,

02:01:57.930 --> 02:01:59.400
you wanna do something new every time,

02:01:59.400 --> 02:02:02.280
then you realize that after
a year or two of doing it,

02:02:02.280 --> 02:02:04.410
you're like, this is
not sustainable at all.

02:02:04.410 --> 02:02:07.080
I need some kind of formula
that I can fall back on

02:02:07.080 --> 02:02:08.250
because I can't always be

02:02:08.250 --> 02:02:11.340
at my peak of creativity every time.

02:02:11.340 --> 02:02:12.173
- Yeah, yeah.
- Yeah.

02:02:12.173 --> 02:02:14.550
- So you guys are like 90%,

02:02:14.550 --> 02:02:15.630
probably going into each episode,

02:02:15.630 --> 02:02:18.544
90% sure where things
are gonna go, you know?

02:02:18.544 --> 02:02:20.220
- Yeah.
- Hmm.

02:02:20.220 --> 02:02:22.763
- Well, going back to the
beginning of this episode, right?

02:02:22.763 --> 02:02:24.605
- We know roughly, we know roughly.

02:02:24.605 --> 02:02:25.501
- We know roughly, yeah.

02:02:25.501 --> 02:02:26.334
